STEP 3.2: Calcination of YBa2Cu3O7 precursor

Purpose: Convert carbonates to oxide phase, remove CO2

Critical Parameters:
- Temperature: 920°C ± 3°C (measured at sample position)
- Ramp rate: 5°C/min (must be uniform)
- Hold time: 12 hours ± 5 min
- Atmosphere: Flowing O2, 1 L/min, 1 atm
- Crucible: Al2O3, pre-fired at 1200°C, 24h

Procedure:
1. Load weighed mixture into Al2O3 crucible (max depth 10mm)
   [VERIFICATION: Mass matches target ±0.001g]
2. Place crucible in furnace center (verify with tape measure)
   [VERIFICATION: Position centered ±5mm]
3. Seal furnace, purge with O2 for 15 min at 5 L/min
   [VERIFICATION: O2 purity >99.999%, flow meter reads 5.0±0.2 L/min]
4. Program furnace: 25°C → 920°C at 5°C/min
   [VERIFICATION: Program verified by second person]
5. Start run, begin logging temperature every 10 sec
   [ACCEPTANCE: Temperature reaches 920±3°C within 184±2 min]
6. Hold at 920°C for 12 hours
   [ACCEPTANCE: Temperature stays 920±3°C for entire hold]
7. Cool naturally to room temperature (furnace off, door closed)
   [ACCEPTANCE: Cooling rate <10°C/min (no thermal shock)]
8. Remove sample, inspect for color change (black → blackish-green)
   [VERIFICATION: Color change observed, no cracks]
9. Grind gently with agate mortar & pestle, 5 min
   [ACCEPTANCE: Particle size <50μm (verify under microscope)]
10. Store in desiccator until next step

Contingencies:
- IF temperature overshoots >926°C → Abort, discard sample, restart
- IF furnace fails to reach 920°C → Check thermocouple, if OK replace element
- IF O2 flow interrupted → Abort, sample may be oxidized incorrectly
- IF sample cracks during cooling → Reduce cooling rate to 3°C/min
- IF color not as expected → Run XRD to verify phase, may need re-calcine

Time Estimate: 14 hours (including setup and cooldown)
Skill Level: Lab technician (training required: 4 hours)
Safety: Use heat-resistant gloves when handling hot crucible, beware of hot surfaces
```

